{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>In the first month.</b> It is written here 'in the wilderness of Sinai,' and it is written there 'in the wilderness of Sinai, on the first day of the month' — just as there it is Rosh Chodesh, so too here it is Rosh Chodesh. Rashi explained here: this passage at the beginning of the book was not stated until Iyyar. You learn from this that there is no chronological order in the Torah. And why did it not begin with this passage? Because it is a disgrace to them, etc. And if you ask: what disgrace is this? After all, in the portion of Bo the verse tied the commandment of Pesach to their entry into the land. One may answer: the disgrace to them is that had they not sinned with the complainers, they would have entered the land in that Iyyar, as it is written, 'ויהי בשנה השנית בחדש השני בעשרים בחודש' etc., and 'Moses said to Hobab: we are traveling to the place' etc., and Rashi explained: immediately, within three days, we enter the land, etc., and they would have made their Pesach offerings in the land. But now that they sinned, they made a month there, as it is written, 'לא יום אחד תאכלו' etc., 'until a month of days.' From there they came to Chatzerot and stayed there seven days for Miriam's quarantine, and they sent the spies, through whom it was decreed upon them to be in the wilderness forty years — and this is the disgrace."], :book :numbers, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:17:06.762761987Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}